From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: voidforge <voidforge@valuz.io>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 23:11:36 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] openarc: embedder: address and payment-card save prompts
 drawn by the shell

Plan C30. The bridge answers the two hooks of the previous patch
(openarc::InstallBridgeAutofillHost) with requests for the tab's dialog
delegate (OACAutofill.h):

- OACAddressSavePrompt (-tab:offerToSaveAddress:): save or update; the
  address in the country's envelope style (name and postal address), email,
  formatted phone, and for an update the changed values (old and new, from
  Chrome's GetProfileDifferenceForUi). Save -> kAccepted, No thanks ->
  kDeclined (Chrome's strikes), dropped -> kIgnored. Prompts that move an
  address into the Google account need a signed-in account, which the app
  never has: answered kAutoDeclined without asking.
- OACCardSavePrompt (-tab:offerToSaveCard:): card, card with security code,
  or security code only; network, last four digits, MM/YY expiry and the
  name on the card (the number stays in the engine). Save -> kAccepted,
  No thanks -> kDeclined, dropped -> kIgnored. An offer without show_prompt
  (the card was refused too often; Chrome would only show an omnibox icon)
  ends as kIgnored.

Saved addresses and cards land in the profile's Web Data (card numbers
encrypted by os_crypt) and come back as rows of the shell-drawn Autofill
dropdown (C13).
